    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Polar Equation of a Radial Line Given an Acute Angle",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/930cb433bd5f972f8b6f7ae12cb937fa84a2f8f30dff9c97f1282a2ead10c3fb.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the ray shown above?",
    "worked_solution": "The counterclockwise angle that the ray makes with the positive $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n2\\pi -\\frac{2\\pi }{7}=\\frac{12\\pi }{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is $\\theta =\\frac{12\\pi }{7}.$",
